// to the wide split-K launch's large grid, not the bigtile leg); at/
// above it, calls mv_fp32_16_hybrid_wide_ilp_shared_half2_atomic_
// branchless_intmask_walign instead of ..._intmask_wide4x. No workspace
// needed (neither callee owns a buffer).
//
// CONFIRMED NOISY/SHAPE-DEPENDENT RESULT on real A100 hardware, NOT
// promoted -- a full square + tall-and-thin sweep vs mv_fp32_16_hybrid_
// wide_ilp_shared_half2_atomic_branchless_intmask_best found real
// regressions at moderate square M (M=4096: -5.3%, M=16384: -0.4%)
// alternating with real wins at nearby sizes (M=6144: +4.0%), and no
// clean threshold predicting which -- except large tall-and-thin M
// (K=4096, M>=262144), which wins consistently and growing (+4.2% to
// +6.6%). See mv_fp32_16_hybrid_wide_ilp_shared_half2_atomic_branchless_
// intmask_walign's own comment (via choose_col_splits_wave_aligned) for
// the full numbers and why. mv_fp32_16_hybrid_wide_ilp_shared_half2_
// atomic_branchless_intmask_best remains the strongest candidate for
